## Why This Is Asked
Explores practical dynamic approximate all-pairs shortest paths (APSP) with shared structure; tests understanding of trade-offs between update costs and query time in batch-dynamic settings.

## Key Concepts
- Batch-dynamic graphs with nonnegative edge weights
- Hub-based distance sketches for approximate APSP
- Amortized analysis across multiple query pairs
- Trade-offs between approximation accuracy ε and computational efficiency
- Incremental shortest path algorithms

## Code Example
```javascript
// Hub-based distance approximation: dist(u,v) ≈ min_h∈H [dist(u,h) + dist(h,v)]

class HubBasedAPSP {
  constructor(graph, epsilon) {
    this.k = Math.ceil((1/epsilon) * Math.log(graph.n));
    this.hubs = this.selectHubs(graph);
    this.distances = new Map(); // hub -> vertex distances
  }

  updateBatch(edges) {
    for (const hub of this.hubs) {
      this.distances.set(hub, this.incrementalDijkstra(hub, edges));
    }
  }

  query(u, v) {
    let minDist = Infinity;
    for (const hub of this.hubs) {
      const dist = this.distances.get(hub).get(u) + 
                   this.distances.get(hub).get(v);
      minDist = Math.min(minDist, dist);
    }
    return minDist;
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical amortized analysis for dynamic frequency tracking, demonstrates how to monitor hot keys efficiently, and contrasts incremental updates with full recomputation.

## Key Concepts
- Amortized analysis for batched updates
- Frequency buckets for O(1) max-frequency queries
- Hash maps for per-label counts
- Sparse vs. dense label domains
- Space-time tradeoff analysis

## Code Example
```javascript
class HotKeyTracker {
  constructor(initialCounts) {
    this.cnt = new Map();
    this.freq = new Map();
    this.maxFreq = 0;
    for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(initialCounts)) {
      this.cnt.set(k, v);
      this.freq.set(v, (this.freq.get(v) || 0) + 1);
      this.maxFreq = Math.max(this.maxFreq, v);
    }
  }

  update(label, delta) {
    const old = this.cnt.get(label) || 0;
    const freqCount = this.freq.get(old) || 0;
    if (freqCount === 1) this.freq.delete(old);
    else this.freq.set(old, freqCount - 1);

    const nw = old + delta;
    this.cnt.set(label, nw);
    this.freq.set(nw, (this.freq.get(nw) || 0) + 1);
    this.maxFreq = Math.max(this.maxFreq, nw);
  }

  hasHotKey(threshold) {
    return this.maxFreq >= threshold;
  }
}
```

